# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  ⇒  /home/medboxne/med-box/media/.htaccess
#
#  ⚠️  This goes in **the media directory itself**, not in public_html.
#
#      The directory reaches the web root through a symbolic link, and putting
#      the protection at the link rather than at its target makes it fall away
#      the moment the serving method changes — moving media to a CDN, or adding
#      a second subdomain pointing at the directory. Here it stays with the
#      files themselves wherever they are served from.
#
#  ⚠️  And this is **a second layer**, not the first.
#
#      The real separation is for private/ not to be under the web root at all —
#      which requires making MEDIA_ROOT overridable by an environment variable
#      (config/settings/base.py:442). As long as that is not done, this file
#      and the public_html rules are all that separates customer documents from the public.
#      A single file deleted by accident during an FTP upload opens all of them.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── No directory indexing ──────────────────────────────────
# Without it the server lists every file in the directory to whoever requests its path
Options -Indexes


# ── No execution — whatever the extension ──────────────────
# ⚠️  A directory users upload into: a file ending in an extension the server
#     executes means remote execution. core/files.py restricts the types to an
#     allow-list at upload, and this is the layer that holds if something gets through.
Options -ExecCGI
RemoveHandler .php .phtml .php3 .php4 .php5 .php7 .php8 .pl .py .cgi .sh .lua
RemoveType .php .phtml .php3 .php4 .php5 .php7 .php8 .pl .py .cgi .sh .lua

<IfModule mod_php.c>
    php_flag engine off
</IfModule>
<IfModule lsapi_module>
    php_flag engine off
</IfModule>


# ── Private paths — blocked by direct path ─────────────────
# ⚠️  The convention already exists in the code: customers/models.py:24 and
#     finance/models.py:29 write under private/ explicitly.
#     mail/ is not beneath it but is equally sensitive (mailing/models.py:567).
#
#     Their legitimate serving through Django reads from disk (FileResponse) rather
#     than through this path — so blocking here breaks nothing.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/media/private/
RedirectMatch 404 ^/media/mail/


# ── Public media caching ───────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️  This applies to the public paths alone: the private paths were answered with
#     404 by the rule above, so they never reach here. And were they to one day —
#     if that rule were deleted — `public` here would mean a shared intermediate
#     cache keeps the file after the signature expires. The two rules are linked:
#     do not delete the first and leave this one.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
    <FilesMatch "\.(pdf|jpe?g|png|webp)$">
        Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=2592000"
    </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
